From 4dbe7572792ccc2d10639fd8c191fc43ca88e08a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter M <petermm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:53:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bsps/riscv: Add ESP32-H2 BSP (riscv/esp32h2db)

Add an ESP32-H2 board support package with rv32imac code and the ilp32 ABI.

- Map the unified 320 KiB HP SRAM at 0x40800000 and reserve 72 KiB at its
  top for the ROM's shared buffers, stack, data and BSS.
- Describe the part's 65 peripheral interrupt sources and route them through
  the interrupt matrix and PLIC, with the Bluetooth, IEEE 802.15.4 and
  coexistence sources on channels of their own.
- Calibrate the fixed 96 MHz BBPLL from the 32 MHz crystal through the analog
  I2C master and select it for a 96 MHz CPU, mirroring ESP-IDF's rtc_clk_init.
  Leave the CPU on the crystal if calibration does not complete, and leave the
  flash interface on the crystal because a direct-boot image has no second
  stage to retime the flash chip for IDF's 64 MHz clock.
- Disable the LP and timer-group watchdogs at the H2's register offsets.
- Run the console from the crystal at 32 MHz: the H2's UART has no SCLK_SEL
  in its clock register and its source stays XTAL.
- Use the H2's I2C and SPI matrix signals, GPIO pad count and register bases.
- Override the BSP's clock init for 96 MHz and keep direct boot and the
  section copy callback enabled.

Signed-off-by: Peter Madsen-Mygdal <petermm@gmail.com>
